---
title: Dulce de Leche Cheesecake
servings: 8
image: https://www.oliviascuisine.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/10/dulce-de-leche-cheesecake.jpg
---

== Crust ==

Combine @butter{1/2%cup}(melted), @graham crackers{1.75%cup}(crushed, about 1.5 wax packages), and @sugar{1/2%cup} in a #food processor{}.

Spread and press into a #10" glass pie pan{} until a crust forms.

== Filling ==

Mix @cream cheese{2%8oz packages}(softened) until smooth.

Mix in @eggs{2}, @brown sugar{1/3%cup}, @sugar{1%tbsp}, @vanilla{1%tsp}, and @sour cream{1/3%cup}.

Split off two spatula scoops of the filling to a separate #bowl. Set aside.

Mix @dulce de leche{1%tbsp} and @cinnamon{1/4%tsp} with the filling. 

Pour half of the filling into the crust, then set the rest aside.

== Swirl ==

To the two spatula scoops we set aside, add @dulce de leche{1/2%cup} and mix until incorporated.

Pour the mixture into the crust and swirl with a skewer until evenly distributed.

Take the remainder of the filling and pour it on top of the swirl layer, spreading evenly.

Bake at 375*F for ~{20%minutes}.

Let stand for ~{15%minutes}.

== Topping ==

Combine @sour cream{1/3%cup}, @dulce de leche{1/3%cup}, @dulce de leche{1%tbsp}, and @vanilla{1%tsp} in a #bowl.

Carefully spread the topping on top of the cheesecake. If you have leftover crumb mixture, sprinkle that on top now.

Return the cheesecake to the oven at 425*F for ~{10%minutes}.

Cool and chill before serving.

> We weren't 100% satisfied with the ratios/style of the original recipe: https://www.piesandtacos.com/dulce-de-leche-cheesecake/#recipe . Thus, we modified our Pumpkin Cheesecake recipe with some details from that recipe to try and create this.